    <innerclass refid="structPermissions" prot="public">Permissions</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>A small type that stores permissions as on/off bits in one byte. (Originally: &quot;Holds a bitmask of authorization bits and the helpers to combine/test them.&quot;). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header defines the <ref refid="structPermissions" kindref="compound">Permissions</ref> struct. It lists the individual rights (like &quot;can read&quot; or &quot;is owner&quot;) as single bits, and provides operators to combine and test those bits. A single value can represent several rights at once.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: Authorization questions (&quot;may this person delete this?&quot;) are answered using these bit masks. <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1a2391c0b165c65deb4ad3ad19ca6dd2aa" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref> and <ref refid="permissionmanager__private_8cpp_1a69fdf8e30d39a5bacfc839feb01dd616" kindref="member">PermissionManagerPrivate</ref> call the helpers here to turn a number stored in the database into a clear yes/no. Without this file there would be no common language for describing rights.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Bit masks and bitwise operators: <ulink url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mask_(computing)">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mask_(computing)</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>C++ bitwise operators: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/operator_arithmetic">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/operator_arithmetic</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>enum class (scoped enumerations): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/enum">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/enum</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>uint8_t (an exact 8-bit integer): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/integer">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/integer</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
